{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium","id":1187863,"title":"Help with fansplat: the Disconcertium","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-20T08:51:47-08:00","id":1187863,"title":"Help with fansplat: the Disconcertium","content":"Go ahead and read this thread if you want to get up to speed: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1185394-the-problem-with-hollow-ones\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...th-hollow-ones</a><br /> <br /> Basically, I'm looking for help developing and fleshing out the Disconcertium, a homebrew independent Craft with a focus on satire, Chaos Magick and Discordianism, with the eventual goal of scraping together a Craftbook on it for when/if OP decides to open up the Storyteller's Vault to Mage.<br /> <br /> Looking for people familiar with the system and setting, obviously.<br /> <br /> Anybody interested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T16:59:23-08:00","id":1188021,"title":"","content":"So is this like an update on the Hollow Ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T18:04:52-08:00","id":1188041,"title":"","content":"Along those lines, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:02:44-08:00","id":1188273,"title":"","content":"So, I guess I'll try to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> First thing's first: Where do we think the Disconcertium fits into the awakened world? What is their organization (such as it is) like?<br /> <br /> Actually, does anyone really care or should I just do this on my own? And, if people are interested, should I open a Google Doc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:42:09-08:00","id":1188337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188273#post1188273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess I'll try to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> First thing's first: Where do we think the Disconcertium fits into the awakened world? What is their organization (such as it is) like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, tough question. For that, I think you have to establish it's background and roots in the modern culture (kinda where they're coming from?) and their &quot;goals&quot; if any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, does anyone really care or should I just do this on my own? And, if people are interested, should I open a Google Doc? </div> </div> </div>I find the idea interesting. Can't promise a serious writin contribution, but I'll gladly discuss ideas as they're coming up. This thread, or a googledoc could work fine, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:16:32-08:00","id":1188345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188337#post1188337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, tough question. For that, I think you have to establish it's background and roots in the modern culture (kinda where they're coming from?) and their &quot;goals&quot; if any.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonable point. I think their place in society is pretty similar to that of real life Discordianism, i.e. fringe artistic and philosophical movements. Connections with real life surrealism, dadaism and satire are probably fair game, as are any particularly fringe/absurd conspiracy theories (e.g. time cube, reptilians). Essentially anything vaguely outlandish or absurdist in the real world that would be too &quot;silly&quot; for other factions to care about. I imagine they would probably be pretty involved in the less politically charged aspects of meme culture, maybe playing both sides in the NWO/VA war as one or the other becomes too radical. Hell, I could imagine them even being behind Creepypastas.<br /> <br /> Their goals would follow a similar trajectory: just trying to get people to stop taking themselves so seriously. Dadaist art displays, flash mobs, parody religions, hoaxes and urban legends, publication of particularly outlandish news stories, all that jazz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:11:57-08:00","id":1188712,"title":"","content":"Right, so I've been thinking: maybe things would be easier to describe if I put out some fiction inspiration so people get the tone and themes the Craft is going for.<br /> <br /> The Principia Discordia<br /> The Illuminatus! Trilogy<br /> Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy<br /> The Phantom Tollbooth<br /> Dirk Gently's Holistic Detective Agency (Both the books and tv series)<br /> John Hodgman's Compendium of Complete World Knowledge<br /> <br /> Here's a link to the doc, also: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Uavwxr8b4w5jnSJaheSons-pP6253vMR7WTTGESJuLQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-22-2018, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:19:16-08:00","id":1188716,"title":"","content":"I feel like many of these elements could be covered by the Virtual Adepts. They have a whole faction of chaos magic, and they could literally rule the world with memes if they tried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:29:37-08:00","id":1188718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188716#post1188716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like many of these elements could be covered by the Virtual Adepts. They have a whole faction of chaos magic, and they could literally rule the world with memes if they tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and most of them would probably be VA's if they joined the traditions (though a lot of them could also pass as Ecstatics or Etherites). But just as the Bata'a aren't Dreamspeakers, the Knights Templar aren't Choristers and the Sisters of Hippolyta aren't Verbenae, the Disconcertium aren't VA's.<br /> <br /> They're a little more complicated than just memes and Chaos Magick. They're absurdism, harnessing the weird and implausible. They are out to <i>prove </i>to people that the world is one big dumb joke that everyone's taking way too seriously.<br /> <br /> They're the only Mages in the world whose paradigm says their magic <i>shouldn't work.</i> The thing is that their paradigm also stresses that the impossible happens regularly and the things that shouldn't work usually do. Its just one more out-of-place puzzle piece in the jumble of contradictions that we call the Tellurian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:05:18-08:00","id":1188728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188718#post1188718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, and most of them would probably be VA's if they joined the traditions (though a lot of them could also pass as Ecstatics or Etherites). But just as the Bata'a aren't Dreamspeakers, the Knights Templar aren't Choristers and the Sisters of Hippolyta aren't Verbenae, the Disconcertium aren't VA's.<br /> <br /> They're a little more complicated than just memes and Chaos Magick. They're absurdism, harnessing the weird and implausible. They are out to <i>prove </i>to people that the world is one big dumb joke that everyone's taking way too seriously.<br /> <br /> They're the only Mages in the world whose paradigm says their magic <i>shouldn't work.</i> The thing is that their paradigm also stresses that the impossible happens regularly and the things that shouldn't work usually do. Its just one more out-of-place puzzle piece in the jumble of contradictions that we call the Tellurian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that those crafts are much older than the traditions they may have been associated with. This by contrast seems much more modern than any other craft or tradition on display.<br /> <br /> A paradigm built on the premise of &quot;Magic doesn't actually work&quot; doesn't seem like something which would invoke enough will to actually change the consensus. I don't know, it all seems like clutching at straws to me really. There's no meat to the belief, it's just mist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T12:23:01-08:00","id":1188960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188728#post1188728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that those crafts are much older than the traditions they may have been associated with. This by contrast seems much more modern than any other craft or tradition on display.<br /> <br /> A paradigm built on the premise of &quot;Magic doesn't actually work&quot; doesn't seem like something which would invoke enough will to actually change the consensus. I don't know, it all seems like clutching at straws to me really. There's no meat to the belief, it's just mist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree. History is replete with gadflies, contrarians, fools, satirists, and absurdists. One of the earliest examples of writing archaeologists have discovered is a &quot;Yo Mama&quot; joke. Voltaire was at once a renowned philosopher and a comedian. Shakespeare wrote bawdy comedies as well as tragedies. The aggressively absurd, the pointedly trivial, it's a part of human existence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Magic doesn't really work&quot; is an oversimplification. In a sane universe, <i>nothing </i>would really work. The more you think about reality, the less sense it makes. It's a sitcom written by hacks and everyone is trying to analyze it like it <i>wasn't </i>created by an idiot.<br /> <br /> They're the inheritors of a noble legacy of ignobility; the leering, jeering ragamuffins paining mustaches and devil horns on all the paintings in the hall of portraits.<br /> <br /> That's the core of the Craft: everyone's delusional, including us. Everything else they do is just a parody of the pomp and circumstance surrounding so-called &quot;enlightenment&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, is it at all realistic to think that, in a world where space marines fight hordes of gremlins inside Wonderland and vampires maneuver against secret societies of ancient wizards for control over a trendy night club, no one has ever stepped back and said to themselves &quot;Y'know, this is kinda' silly&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T12:43:51-08:00","id":1188963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188960#post1188960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I respectfully disagree. History is replete with gadflies, contrarians, fools, satirists, and absurdists. One of the earliest examples of writing archaeologists have discovered is a &quot;Yo Mama&quot; joke. Voltaire was at once a renowned philosopher and a comedian. Shakespeare wrote bawdy comedies as well as tragedies. The aggressively absurd, the pointedly trivial, it's a part of human existence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Magic doesn't really work&quot; is an oversimplification. In a sane universe, <i>nothing </i>would really work. The more you think about reality, the less sense it makes. It's a sitcom written by hacks and everyone is trying to analyze it like it <i>wasn't </i>created by an idiot.<br /> <br /> They're the inheritors of a noble legacy of ignobility; the leering, jeering ragamuffins paining mustaches and devil horns on all the paintings in the hall of portraits.<br /> <br /> That's the core of the Craft: everyone's delusional, including us. Everything else they do is just a parody of the pomp and circumstance surrounding so-called &quot;enlightenment&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, is it at all realistic to think that, in a world where space marines fight hordes of gremlins inside Wonderland and vampires maneuver against secret societies of ancient wizards for control over a trendy night club, no one has ever stepped back and said to themselves &quot;Y'know, this is kinda' silly&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, so if the world is utter nonsense, how does one bring about their influence upon it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T12:59:09-08:00","id":1188968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188963#post1188963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ok, so if the world is utter nonsense, how does one bring about their influence upon it?</div> </div> </div> </div>By accepting the fundamental silliness of it all. The world plays nice with those who get the joke. Other people could do what they do too, if they'd stop putting restrictions on what's possible. They accept that the laws of physics are just suggestions, that God is an idiot who's not really paying attention and that nature is just a series of random events that people sometimes ascribe meaning to.<br /> <br /> In essence, they acknowledge the fundamental improbability of all things. The whys and hows of the world don't really make a ton of sense if you step back and really take a hard look at them. Once you realize that the impossible is already happening around you every day, that everything you see is already a miracle of contrivance, what's to stop you from doing what most people call &quot;impossible&quot;?<br /> <br /> Who says the Time Cube can't be true? You can't <i>prove </i>the Flying Spaghetti Monster isn't real! If dragons once walked the earth, why not an Invisible Pink Unicorn?<br /> <br /> Not to beat a dead horse, but I think that reading the Principia Discordia would really offer some clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:22:52-08:00","id":1188975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188968#post1188968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By accepting the fundamental silliness of it all. The world plays nice with those who get the joke. Other people could do what they do too, if they'd stop putting restrictions on what's possible. They accept that the laws of physics are just suggestions, that God is an idiot who's not really paying attention and that nature is just a series of random events that people sometimes ascribe meaning to.<br /> <br /> In essence, they acknowledge the fundamental improbability of all things. The whys and hows of the world don't really make a ton of sense if you step back and really take a hard look at them. Once you realize that the impossible is already happening around you every day, that everything you see is already a miracle of contrivance, what's to stop you from doing what most people call &quot;impossible&quot;?<br /> <br /> Who says the Time Cube can't be true? You can't <i>prove </i>the Flying Spaghetti Monster isn't real! If dragons once walked the earth, why not an Invisible Pink Unicorn?<br /> <br /> Not to beat a dead horse, but I think that reading the Principia Discordia would really offer some clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So how do they explain away why all the serious mages are able to do their magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:30:11-08:00","id":1188977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188975#post1188975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So how do they explain away why all the serious mages are able to do their magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, you <i>can</i> call upon the will of God (that doofus) or unleash their inner beast or build a death ray. Are you gonna' say it's impossible? Of course not! That's the opposite of what the Disconcertium wants to do!<br /> <br /> The thing about serious Mages is that they recognize that <i>some &quot;</i>impossible&quot; things are actually possible, but not all of them. A Disconcertian <i>could </i>just throw a fireball with a chant and some chalk circles, but that runs the risk of someone taking it seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:55:23-08:00","id":1188992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188977#post1188977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sure, you <i>can</i> call upon the will of God (that doofus) or unleash their inner beast or build a death ray. Are you gonna' say it's impossible? Of course not! That's the opposite of what the Disconcertium wants to do!<br /> <br /> The thing about serious Mages is that they recognize that <i>some &quot;</i>impossible&quot; things are actually possible, but not all of them. A Disconcertian <i>could </i>just throw a fireball with a chant and some chalk circles, but that runs the risk of someone taking it seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand... So their whole schtick is you have to not take things seriously in order to do magic, yet they admit that serious mages taking their magic seriously are capable of doing magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:59:11-08:00","id":1188996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188992#post1188992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand... So their whole schtick is you have to not take things seriously in order to do magic, yet they admit that serious mages taking their magic seriously are capable of doing magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you misunderstand. You don't <i>have </i>to not take things seriously, it just opens up more possibilities. To a Disconcertian, nobody <i>has </i>to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:04:35-08:00","id":1189000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188996#post1188996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you misunderstand. You don't <i>have </i>to not take things seriously, it just opens up more possibilities. To a Disconcertian, nobody <i>has </i>to do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nobody has to do anything, what separates a mage from a sleeper? Heck, how do sorcerers fit in to this ideology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:13:40-08:00","id":1189005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189000#post1189000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If nobody has to do anything, what separates a mage from a sleeper? Heck, how do sorcerers fit in to this ideology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepers are people that just don't get how ridiculous things are. &quot;Enlightenment&quot;, such as it is, comes from the realization that the bounds of reality aren't nearly as defined as you think. That the world is <i>weirder </i>than you think.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are people that understand this in theory, but just can't let go of their attachment to the serious world and some of the rules they think it operates on. Try as they might, they can't help but see order in the chaos. When they not only realize, but truly <i>understand </i>that the world is a big dumb mess, they Awaken.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, this is really helping me flesh them out! Thanks!<br /> <br /> Finding new avenues of thought and developing through arguing with someone about how things do or don't work and how seriously to take them. There's nothing more Disconcertian than that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T15:06:51-08:00","id":1189022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189005#post1189005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepers are people that just don't get how ridiculous things are. &quot;Enlightenment&quot;, such as it is, comes from the realization that the bounds of reality aren't nearly as defined as you think. That the world is <i>weirder </i>than you think.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are people that understand this in theory, but just can't let go of their attachment to the serious world and some of the rules they think it operates on. Try as they might, they can't help but see order in the chaos. When they not only realize, but truly <i>understand </i>that the world is a big dumb mess, they Awaken.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, this is really helping me flesh them out! Thanks!<br /> <br /> Finding new avenues of thought and developing through arguing with someone about how things do or don't work and how seriously to take them. There's nothing more Disconcertian than that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It still doesn't have an internal logic to it. I can get behind the idea that the world is chaotic, I can also understand the idea that if you embrace the tenemant of chaos then you can imbue your own order into it. But you're denying that even this happens. There can't be any kind of order otherwise it's not truly chaotic. And if it is truly chaotic, then it's fundamentally inaccessible to everyone, and thus beyond control. How can you do magic without any kind of control?<br /> <br /> If &quot;stuff just happens&quot; then there is no difference between a mage and a sleeper, stuff is just happening, the mage isn't doing anything but pointing it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T15:16:32-08:00","id":1189027,"title":"","content":"You can create small-scale meaningless order, but in a cosmic sense your actions creating your desired pattern are a product of cosmic randomness that you are an expression of, and thus are not a change from the cosmic absurdity, just one manifestation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T15:29:29-08:00","id":1189028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189027#post1189027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can create small-scale meaningless order, but in a cosmic sense your actions creating your desired pattern are a product of cosmic randomness that you are an expression of, and thus are not a change from the cosmic absurdity, just one manifestation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;become one with the weirdness, and create your own meaningless imprint on the universe&quot;. I can get behind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T16:38:59-08:00","id":1189042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1188975#post1188975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So how do they explain away why all the serious mages are able to do their magic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each piece of magic was possible due to the inherent absurdity of the world manifesting at the right time with the right (brief flash of) insight. Each magical philosophy, if examined closely, contains elements of absurdity. Science thinks it's immune, but somehow we drift from Newtonian physics to Quantum theory. Each question asked reveals an answer...that leads to more and more questions. Thus, even science, meant to add clarity and banish the sense of absurdity, adds questions and highlights the absurdity. <br /> <br /> These guys could be VA's, or Cultists of Ecstasy, or Akashics...but they're digging deeper into the absurdity and embracing the instinctive &quot;just do&quot; that ties all of these movements together. They don't have a group purpose, unless it's to lead mages and others to realize that divisions are ultimately futile and that we're better off working together to hash things out. They know they won't get consensus changed, and if they do, it was probably by accident. They're not thinking about consensus; they don't see the purpose of the War For Reality in the first place. And thus, they come out ahead by not playing the game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T17:43:22-08:00","id":1189056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189028#post1189028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;become one with the weirdness, and create your own meaningless imprint on the universe&amp;quot;. I can get behind that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well part of absurdism and it\u2019s intersection with chaos theory is that you\u2019re an expression of random probabilities no matter what you do. There is no being more \u201cone with it\u201d or not. There is only being aware of it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T20:21:22-08:00","id":1189100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189042#post1189042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Each piece of magic was possible due to the inherent absurdity of the world manifesting at the right time with the right (brief flash of) insight. Each magical philosophy, if examined closely, contains elements of absurdity. Science thinks it's immune, but somehow we drift from Newtonian physics to Quantum theory. Each question asked reveals an answer...that leads to more and more questions. Thus, even science, meant to add clarity and banish the sense of absurdity, adds questions and highlights the absurdity.<br /> <br /> These guys could be VA's, or Cultists of Ecstasy, or Akashics...but they're digging deeper into the absurdity and embracing the instinctive &quot;just do&quot; that ties all of these movements together. They don't have a group purpose, unless it's to lead mages and others to realize that divisions are ultimately futile and that we're better off working together to hash things out. They know they won't get consensus changed, and if they do, it was probably by accident. They're not thinking about consensus; they don't see the purpose of the War For Reality in the first place. And thus, they come out ahead by not playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exactly. Thank you.<br /> <br /> So now that we have that hashed out, let's look at the &quot;organization&quot; itself. How does it view the rest of magickal society? How about the Night Folk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-23-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T01:12:44-08:00","id":1189150,"title":"","content":"Probably as flipently as they view everything else.<br /> They would probably has a much more positive view on malkavians and marauders, possibly even seeing them as proof of concept.<br /> Regarding the spirit world, the wyld would definetly bee their patron of choice, even if just conceptually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T11:10:33-08:00","id":1189267,"title":"","content":"I'm just keeping an eye on this, as I've had a similar idea for awhile now, but never committed it to anything. I'll try to have something up soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:57:15-08:00","id":1189302,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Looking forward to seeing what you guys bring to the table!<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm working on writing up a spread on the Disco's, as if they had been in a corebook. Should at least give us a jumping off point. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:29:24-08:00","id":1189417,"title":"","content":"Hey kids! Time for a preview: a good old-fashioned White Wolf &quot;Stereotypes&quot; section, just like mama used to make!<br /> <br /> <b>The Traditions:</b> Wait, I've heard this one. It's the one about a bunch of doofuses that think they're accomplishing something, right?<br /> <br /> <b>-The Akashic Brotherhood:</b> Now you too can achieve nonspecific enlightenment, for the low, low price of a lifetime of doing absolutely nothing! Well sign me the fuck up!<br /> <br /> <b>-The Celestial Chorus:</b> Oh, they've been touched by His Noodly Appendages alright.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Cult of Ecstacy:</b> These guys are dangerously close to getting it. If they got any closer, we might be out of a job!<br /> <br /> <b>-The Dreamspeakers:</b> I don't get it. They've seen the stupidity that is the spirit world and they still approach it with stone-faced seriousness. What is their deal?<br /> <br /> <b>-The Euthanatos:</b> AHAHAHAHAHAHA!<br /> <br /> <b>-The Order of Hermes:</b> Wait, I'm not done laughing at the Euthanatos. AHAHAHAHAHAHA! But seriously, these guys manage to take wizardry and make it dull. Irritate whenever possible.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Society of Ether: </b>I just found out that they're not joking. That's hilarious.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Verbena:</b> I thought witches were supposed to live in gingerbread houses! What is this &quot;Earthsoul&quot; shit?<br /> <br /> <b>-The Virtual Adepts:</b> They're like us, but with more 1337 speak and less melanin. Great if you're into that kind of thing, you weirdo.<br /> <br /> <b>The Technocracy:</b> The greatest trick Eris ever played was convincing the world she didn't exist.<br /> <br /> <b>-Iteration X:</b> Hey, if I say &quot;I always lie&quot;, will you guys explode?<br /> <br /> <b>-The New World Order:</b> Pfft. Small time. They probably don't even know about the Cloud People.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Progenitors:</b> Booo. Make more turkey-spiders! Boooooooo.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Syndicate:</b> Bless you. Infomercials are some of the best TV out there.<br /> <br /> <b>-The Void Engineers:</b> Hey, if you guys find a teapot out there, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:05:09-08:00","id":1189424,"title":"","content":"I just realised something really problematic from a ST perspective if you allow the players to take this as their craft. It gives the player free reign to be as obnoxious as possible with the &quot;get out of jail free&quot; comment of &quot;What? I'm just roleplaying!&quot;<br /> <br /> From experience, this kind of thing has the potential to frustrate everyone in the room.<br /> <br /> Either that, or you need the kind of players who wouldn't have taken the story seriously in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-25-2018, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:11:53-08:00","id":1189425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1187863-help-with-fansplat-the-disconcertium?p=1189424#post1189424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realised something really problematic from a ST perspective if you allow the players to take this as their craft. It gives the player free reign to be as obnoxious as possible with the &quot;get out of jail free&quot; comment of &quot;What? I'm just roleplaying!&quot;<br /> <br /> From experience, this kind of thing has the potential to frustrate everyone in the room.<br /> <br /> Either that, or you need the kind of players who wouldn't have taken the story seriously in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, you raise a good point. Anyone have any idea how to fix that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}